        "subject": "LU-21061 lfs: add --pool to setdirstripe and mkdir",
        "message": "LU-21061 lfs: add --pool to setdirstripe and mkdir\n\nA directory layout cannot name a pool.  lfs setdirstripe has no pool\noption, and a pool given through llapi is lost on the way:\nverify_dir_param() cuts \"<fsname>.<pool>\" down to \"<fsname>\" in the\ncaller's string, lmv_unpack_user_md() drops the pool of a default\nLMV, and llite clears it when it sends the parent default with mkdir.\n\nAdd -p/--pool to lfs setdirstripe and lfs mkdir.  Strip the fsname\nwithout changing the caller's string, and when the pool lists MDTs,\nrequire that -i names MDTs of the pool.  Keep the pool of a default\nLMV on the client and send it with mkdir.  The MDTs do not use the\npool yet.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: Ib4356120e046ac269488034f261923162f84899a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
